-- title:
--   Ramification index one makes π a uniformiser at q
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ and $B$ be Dedekind domains (in the same universe) with an $A$-algebra structure on $B$, let $\pi \in A$, and let $\mathfrak p$ be a maximal ideal of $A$ with $\mathfrak p = (\pi)$. Let $\mathfrak q$ be a maximal ideal of $B$, assumed non-zero, such that the ideal $\mathfrak p B$ generated by the image of $\mathfrak p$ under $A \to B$ is contained in $\mathfrak q$, and assume the ramification index $e(\mathfrak q \mid \mathfrak p)$, in the form `Ideal.ramificationIdx' p q`, equals $1$. Let $L$ be a field which is a fraction field of $B$, equipped with compatible $A$- and $B$-algebra structures forming a scalar tower $A \to B \to L$, and let $z \in L$ be non-zero. Then there are an integer $n$ and elements $b, s \in B$, both outside $\mathfrak q$, such that in $L$ one has $$z \cdot s = \pi^{\,n} \, b,$$ where $\pi$, $b$ and $s$ are read in $L$ through the respective structure maps and $\pi^{\,n}$ is an integer power (possibly negative) of the image of $\pi$.
--
--   The statement records that under $e(\mathfrak q\mid\mathfrak p)=1$ a generator $\pi$ of $\mathfrak p$ is a uniformiser at $\mathfrak q$, so that every non-zero element of the fraction field of $B$ is $\pi^n$ times a unit of the local ring $B_{\mathfrak q}$, with numerator and denominator taken prime to $\mathfrak q$. It is used in the proof of [`ValuationSubring.exists_ne_zero_and_div_mem_of_forall_smul_eq_imp_apply_eq`](thm.html#ValuationSubring.exists_ne_zero_and_div_mem_of_forall_smul_eq_imp_apply_eq), where valuations have to be compared with powers of a fixed element of the base.
